# Generated by scripts/publish.sh in tuta-alias_stage. Do not edit here.
#
# bin/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the published binary is built from
# the stage commit this tree came from and is committed with it.


# Per-machine state that must never be committed. .gitleaks.toml refuses the
# same list on the way to git, in case one of these is added with -f or lands
# under a name this list does not predict.
*.session.json
session.json
api-token
vault.json
tuta-alias.conf
plus-aliases.json
alias-notes.json
client-version
*.log
*.kdbx
.env
.private/

# Agent worktrees. An agent that edits files gets its own copy of the repo
# under here, so its work in progress cannot collide with anyone else's; the
# copies are temporary and never part of the project.
.claude/worktrees/

# Scratch probes. A review that wants to know what the code really does
# writes a throwaway test, runs it and deletes it; one of those was swept into
# a commit by `git add -A` once already. The zz_ prefix keeps them out of the
# index and sorts them last while they exist.
zz_*_test.go

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
